---
/**
 * Terms of Use for the free GeoReady services.
 *
 * Scope: the public site geoready.dev (free audit, tools, guides, public
 * audit API) and the audit service the GeoReady WordPress plugin calls on
 * app.geoready.dev. Paid plans on app.geoready.dev are deliberately out of
 * scope: they need their own terms (billing, renewal, withdrawal, refunds).
 *
 * Every factual statement below was checked against the code at the time of
 * writing (engine web app, platform WordPress endpoint, plugin). Rate-limit
 * numbers are intentionally not quoted: they are server configuration and
 * change without a new version of this page.
 *
 * The governing-law, liability and consumer-law sections are filled in and the
 * draft banner is off. They mirror the app.geoready.dev subscription terms
 * (Italian law, courts of Chieti, consumer protections preserved); have counsel
 * confirm them if the operator wants a formal review.
 */
import Shell from '../components/Shell.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 14, 2026';
const isDraft = false;

/* Shared class strings, identical to the ones used on /privacy/. */
const link =
  'text-pass-deep underline decoration-rail underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-pass-deep';
const h2 = 'mb-3 font-head text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink';
const strong = 'font-semibold text-ink';
---

<Shell
  title="Terms of Use — GeoReady"
  description="Terms for the free GeoReady services: the audit and tools on geoready.dev and the audit service used by the GeoReady WordPress plugin."
  canonical="https://geoready.dev/terms/"
>
  <div class="bg-paper">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 md:py-16">
      {isDraft && (
        <div class="mb-8 rounded-[4px] border border-warn bg-warn-wash p-4 text-sm text-ink" role="note">
          <strong class={strong}>Draft for review.</strong> This page has not been approved yet.
          Sections marked “To be decided” need the operator’s decision before publication.
        </div>
      )}

      <header class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
          <h1 class="font-head text-3xl font-extrabold leading-tight tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink md:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ink-mute">GeoReady · Terms of Use</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-mute">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          These terms apply when you use the free GeoReady services: the audit, tools and guides
          on <strong class={strong}>geoready.dev</strong>, its public audit API, and the audit service
          that the <strong class={strong}>GeoReady WordPress plugin</strong> calls on app.geoready.dev.
          How we handle personal data is described in the{' '}
          <a href="/privacy/" class={link}>Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-10 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Who provides the service</h2>
          <p class="mb-1 text-sm"><strong class={strong}>Juan Camilo Auriti</strong></p>
          <p class="text-sm">
            Email: <a href="mailto:info@geoready.dev" class={link}>info@geoready.dev</a>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>What these terms do not cover</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm">
            <li>
              <strong class={strong}>Paid plans</strong> on app.geoready.dev (subscriptions, billing,
              monitoring) are governed by separate terms that you accept when you subscribe.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class={strong}>The open-source code.</strong> The GEO Optimizer engine is
              released under the{' '}
              <a href="https://github.com/Auriti-Labs/geo-optimizer-skill/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class={link}>MIT License</a>{' '}
              and the WordPress plugin under the GPL. If you run that code yourself, its licence
              applies, not these terms. These terms cover the hosted services we run.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>How the audit works</h2>
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm">
            When you submit a URL, our servers request the publicly available pages and files of
            that site (for example the home page, robots.txt and llms.txt), analyse them and return
            a score with recommendations. We do not log in to your site, so password-protected
            pages cannot be audited, and addresses on private networks or local hosts are refused.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm">
            To keep the service available for everyone, requests are rate-limited, both per
            visitor and per audited site, and recent results can be served from a short-lived
            cache instead of a new audit. The limits are not part of these terms and may change.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>What the score is, and what it is not</h2>
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm">
            The score and the recommendations are produced automatically from the content your
            site serves at the moment of the audit, using the method published on the{' '}
            <a href="/methodology/" class={link}>methodology page</a>. They describe how ready the
            page is to be read by AI search systems.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm">
            They are <strong class={strong}>not a guarantee</strong> that any AI system, search engine
            or assistant will cite, rank or mention your site, and they are not legal, security or
            accessibility advice. A site can change between two audits, and so can the systems the
            score is about. Check a recommendation before you apply it to a production site.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Using the service fairly</h2>
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm">You agree not to:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm">
            <li>submit URLs you are not entitled to have analysed;</li>
            <li>
              use the audit to put load on a third-party site, or try to get around the rate
              limits, for example by rotating IP addresses or running many installs against the
              same site;
            </li>
            <li>try to make our servers reach private networks or internal addresses;</li>
            <li>interfere with the service, probe it for vulnerabilities outside a disclosed
              report, or use it in a way that breaks the law.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
            We may refuse, limit or block requests that do any of these things, without notice.
            Security issues can be reported privately to the address above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>The WordPress plugin</h2>
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm">
            When you run an audit from the plugin, it sends the address of your site, a flag that
            says whether you allowed benchmark statistics, and the plugin and WordPress versions.
            The versions are checked for format and not stored. The plugin also sends its own user
            agent, <code class="font-mono text-[12px]">GeoReady-WordPress/&lt;version&gt;</code>.
          </p>
          <p class="mb-3 text-sm">
            The benchmark setting is <strong class={strong}>off by default</strong>. If you turn it on,
            each audit also saves a pseudonymised record used only for aggregate statistics: a
            keyed hash of the domain instead of the domain itself, its top-level domain, the date,
            the engine version, the scores and the check results. The record is pseudonymised,
            not anonymous. Turning the setting off stops new records from being saved.
          </p>
          <p class="text-sm">
            The files the plugin generates on your site (llms.txt, ai.txt, summary.json) are built
            from your own published content and stay on your server. You are responsible for what
            they publish.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Availability and changes</h2>
          <p class="text-sm">
            The free services are provided as they are, without a service-level commitment. We
            may change, suspend or discontinue any of them, including the API the plugin uses.
            When a change affects the plugin, we will say so in the plugin’s changelog.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Your content and ours</h2>
          <p class="text-sm">
            Your site and its content remain yours; analysing them gives us no rights over them.
            The GeoReady name, the site design and the written guides belong to the operator.
            The open-source code is covered by its own licence, as stated above.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Liability</h2>
          <p class="text-sm">
            The free services are provided as they are, without warranty. A higher GEO score is not
            a promise of citations or traffic, and we do not guarantee the audit is free of errors or
            always available. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or
            consequential loss, or for decisions you take based on a free audit. Nothing here limits
            liability that cannot be limited by law — for wilful misconduct or gross negligence, for
            death or personal injury, or the mandatory rights of consumers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Governing law and disputes</h2>
          <p class="text-sm">
            These terms are governed by Italian law, and the courts of Chieti have jurisdiction. If
            you use the service as a consumer, the mandatory consumer protections of your country of
            residence still apply, regardless of this clause.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class={h2}>Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p class="text-sm">
            We update these terms when the services change, and the date at the top says when.
            Using a service after a change means the updated terms apply from then on.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "name": "Terms of Use — GeoReady",
    "description": "Terms for the free GeoReady services: the audit and tools on geoready.dev and the audit service used by the GeoReady WordPress plugin.",
    "url": "https://geoready.dev/terms/",
    "isPartOf": {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      "name": "GeoReady",
      "url": "https://geoready.dev"
    }
  })} />
</Shell>
